WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.015 --> 00:00:04.848
Hello and welcome back

00:00:04.848 --> 00:00:07.197
to Arya Nagarjuna.

00:00:07.197 --> 00:00:08.447
And here we go.

00:00:10.195 --> 00:00:13.422
And we're going to go
till 5:25, right Tim?

00:00:13.422 --> 00:00:15.411
All right, good.

00:00:15.411 --> 00:00:18.419
We had 7 options for causes and effects

00:00:18.419 --> 00:00:21.359
that were basically separate.

00:00:21.359 --> 00:00:23.878
And then here's option number five.

00:00:23.878 --> 00:00:26.440
The result being triggered,

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.083
does it have a nature of its own

00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:31.110
or is it devoid of such a nature?

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:34.619
So now, notice that they've switched

00:00:34.619 --> 00:00:36.763
the meaning of voidness here?

00:00:36.763 --> 00:00:41.763
Before, voidness meant is the
cause devoid of the result.

00:00:41.907 --> 00:00:44.463
And now we're asking,

00:00:44.463 --> 00:00:47.853
is the result devoid
of a nature of its own?

00:00:47.853 --> 00:00:51.787
So different devoids.

00:00:51.787 --> 00:00:54.470
,'BRAS BU MI STONG SKYE MI 'GYUR,

00:00:55.496 --> 00:00:57.837
,MI STONG 'GAG PAR MI 'GYUR RO,

00:00:57.837 --> 00:01:01.095
,MI STONG DE NI MI 'GAGS DANG,

00:01:01.095 --> 00:01:03.453
,MA SKYES PAR YANG 'GYUR PA YIN,

00:01:05.053 --> 00:01:08.236
,'BRAS BU MI STONG SKYE MI 'GYUR,

00:01:09.363 --> 00:01:11.946
There cannot be a starting

00:01:11.946 --> 00:01:15.196
if the thing is not devoid of a result.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.193
Let me think about this.

00:01:20.287 --> 00:01:22.469
I think that first line might be talking

00:01:22.469 --> 00:01:24.488
about the old kind of devoid.

00:01:24.488 --> 00:01:27.290
Let's go to the commentary.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:29.498
'BRAS BU SKYE BA RANG BZHIN
GYIS STONG PA'AM MI STONG

00:01:29.498 --> 00:01:31.814
GANG ZHIG SKYE GRANG,

00:01:31.814 --> 00:01:35.142
By the way, that SKYE GRANG

00:01:35.142 --> 00:01:39.693
in the first line is a new
expression. I've never seen it.

00:01:39.693 --> 00:01:42.943
But he started to use it over and over

00:01:43.992 --> 00:01:46.409
and now it's clear. It means,

00:01:48.161 --> 00:01:50.893
"I'll give you a couple
choices, you choose one."

00:01:50.893 --> 00:01:52.105
So SKYE GRANG means

00:01:52.105 --> 00:01:53.071
I'll give you a couple choices,

00:01:53.071 --> 00:01:55.541
you tell me which one you like.

00:01:55.541 --> 00:01:59.182
'BRAS BU SKYE BA RANG BZHIN
GYIS STONG PA'AM MI STONG

00:01:59.182 --> 00:02:02.356
Oh, that was the line that
was messed up in the carving.

00:02:03.773 --> 00:02:05.723
The carving said the same thing

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:08.737
for options four and five.

00:02:09.935 --> 00:02:13.650
So one of them had to be
wrong, and it's this one.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.502
And what it really should say

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:21.502
is 'BRAS BU SKYE BA RANG
BZHIN GYIS STONG PA'AM

00:02:21.658 --> 00:02:23.849
"Is the growing of the result,

00:02:23.849 --> 00:02:25.797
"is the starting of the result,

00:02:25.797 --> 00:02:29.504
"is the growing of the result
empty of its own nature or not?"

00:02:29.504 --> 00:02:32.254
You tell me what you think.

00:02:32.254 --> 00:02:36.146
Now, he's not saying the
cause is empty or not

00:02:36.146 --> 00:02:38.157
or the result is empty or not.

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:40.861
He's talking about the
growing of the result,

00:02:40.861 --> 00:02:44.417
is it empty or not. Got it? Different.

00:02:44.417 --> 00:02:48.229
Is the growing of the result empty or not?

00:02:48.229 --> 00:02:52.146
DE LA 'BRAS BU RANG BZHIN GYIS
YOD PAS MI STONG PA CHOS CAN,

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:55.806
Let's consider a result,

00:02:58.014 --> 00:03:02.405
which was not empty of
having its own nature.

00:03:02.405 --> 00:03:05.072
Let's take the case of a result,

00:03:05.988 --> 00:03:08.278
which was not empty of its own nature.

00:03:08.278 --> 00:03:10.337
SKYE BAR MI 'GYUR BAR THAL,

00:03:10.337 --> 00:03:15.337
It cannot start because 
RTEN 'BREL MA YIN

00:03:16.616 --> 00:03:17.898
RTEN 'BREL MA YIN

00:03:17.898 --> 00:03:19.690
It's not dependent origination.

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:22.168
It would not exhibit
dependent origination.

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:23.423
So, there he's just,

00:03:23.423 --> 00:03:27.456
he's just used it as a
reason in an argument,

00:03:27.456 --> 00:03:32.456
but it's a profound principle
that he's talking about.

00:03:32.681 --> 00:03:33.681
What is it?

00:03:37.382 --> 00:03:41.320
If something were dependent origination,

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.986
it could not have its own nature.

00:03:44.986 --> 00:03:47.526
Sorry, it would have to be
empty of its own nature.

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:50.747
If something were dependent origination,

00:03:50.747 --> 00:03:54.417
it would have to be
empty of its own nature.

00:03:54.417 --> 00:03:58.478
DE 'DRA BA'I MI
STONG PA DE NI CHOS CAN

00:03:58.478 --> 00:04:02.977
If it were not empty of its own nature,

00:04:02.977 --> 00:04:06.012
if it were not empty of its own nature,

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:08.366
it couldn't be dependent origination,

00:04:08.366 --> 00:04:11.013
and it couldn't 
'GAG PA

00:04:11.013 --> 00:04:12.753
Which means what?

00:04:12.753 --> 00:04:14.985
It could never stop.

00:04:14.985 --> 00:04:16.343
Because RANG BZHIN GYIS GRUB PA'I PHYIR

00:04:16.343 --> 00:04:18.079
that's sort of a cheap argument:

00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:21.329
because it has its own nature. Thanks.

00:04:24.052 --> 00:04:27.872
By the way, he has repeated
over and over again

00:04:27.872 --> 00:04:30.220
that if something had its own nature,

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.995
it could never come to a stop,

00:04:32.995 --> 00:04:37.107
because then it would lose
its nature. That's all.

00:04:37.107 --> 00:04:39.338
It's been a repeated argument

00:04:39.338 --> 00:04:43.168
that if something had its
own nature, it couldn't die

00:04:43.168 --> 00:04:45.476
because that means its
nature would have to change

00:04:45.476 --> 00:04:48.066
and it wouldn't be its own nature anymore.

00:04:48.066 --> 00:04:51.500
So things that have their
own self-existent nature

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.219
could never stop.

00:04:53.219 --> 00:04:54.981
Because then they would be different

00:04:54.981 --> 00:04:57.058
from what they were before,
and that's not possible

00:04:57.058 --> 00:05:00.149
if a thing has its own nature.

00:05:01.423 --> 00:05:04.248
'GAG PAR MI 'GYUR BAR THAL,
RANG BZHIN GYIS GRUB PA'I PHYIR,

00:05:04.248 --> 00:05:06.986
KHYAB STE, RANG BZHIN LA
LDOG PA MED PA'I PHYIR,

00:05:06.986 --> 00:05:08.736
Here's the punchline.

00:05:13.255 --> 00:05:16.039
If something is something's nature,

00:05:16.039 --> 00:05:19.819
its true nature, it cannot be modified.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:22.375
That nature cannot be modified.

00:05:22.375 --> 00:05:23.609
It cannot. 
LDOG PA means

00:05:23.609 --> 00:05:26.276
to turn it back, stop it.

00:05:27.257 --> 00:05:30.615
It could not be changed or stopped,

00:05:30.615 --> 00:05:32.462
if it were a true nature.

00:05:32.462 --> 00:05:34.940
If it were an inherent
nature, it couldn't be stopped

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:39.523
because then the thing wouldn't
be what it was anymore.

00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:45.384
You couldn't cut the cancer out
without killing the patient,

00:05:45.384 --> 00:05:47.332
something like that.

00:05:47.332 --> 00:05:48.932
All right.

00:05:48.932 --> 00:05:51.799
DE BZHIN DU MI STONG PAR 'DOD
NA NI MI 'THAD DE, DE NI

00:05:51.799 --> 00:05:54.715
MA 'GAGS PA DANG MA SKYES PAR
YANG 'GYUR BA YIN PA'I PHYIR,

00:06:01.225 --> 00:06:03.475
If you deny that the result

00:06:04.423 --> 00:06:07.673
could have any nature of its own,

00:06:08.574 --> 00:06:11.122
then it could never stop or start.

00:06:11.122 --> 00:06:12.989
It would have to have some nature,

00:06:12.989 --> 00:06:15.001
but not a self-existent nature.

00:06:15.001 --> 00:06:17.001
Not an immutable nature.

00:06:18.271 --> 00:06:22.531
'BRAS BU RANG BZHIN GYIS YOD
PAS STONG PA NI CHOS CAN,

00:06:22.531 --> 00:06:25.687
Let's take the fact that
the result doesn't exist

00:06:25.687 --> 00:06:27.884
through any nature of its own.

00:06:27.884 --> 00:06:30.317
JI LTAR NGO BO NYID KYIS
SKYE BAR 'GYUR ZHING JI

00:06:30.317 --> 00:06:33.108
LTAR NA NGO BO NYID KYIS 'GAG
PAR 'GYUR BAR NI MI 'THAD DE,

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:38.448
If the result were empty
of any nature of its own,

00:06:38.448 --> 00:06:41.490
it could never start and never stop.

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:44.471
'THAD DE, RANG BZHIN
GYIS STONG PA'I PHYIR,

00:06:44.471 --> 00:06:48.816
Because it wouldn't have
any nature to change.

00:06:48.816 --> 00:06:53.241
If it had its own self-existent nature,

00:06:53.241 --> 00:06:56.483
it could never stop especially.

00:06:56.483 --> 00:06:58.505
If it didn't have any nature at all,

00:06:58.505 --> 00:07:00.899
it couldn't start or stop.

00:07:00.899 --> 00:07:05.149
So it has a nature, but
not a self-existent nature.

00:07:06.381 --> 00:07:10.513
I don't like my picture so
much, I'm going to skip it.

00:07:10.513 --> 00:07:13.063
'BRAS BU RANG BZHIN GYIS STONG
PAR 'DOD PA DE YANG NGO BO

00:07:13.063 --> 00:07:14.587
NYID KYIS MA 'GAGS PA DANG MA
SKYES PAR YANG THAL BAR 'GYUR

00:07:14.587 --> 00:07:16.529
BA LA NI KHO BO CAG NI 'DOD
KYANG KHYED DE LTAR MI 'DOD DE

00:07:16.529 --> 00:07:19.248
'GAL BA YIN NO,,

00:07:19.248 --> 00:07:21.405
Yes, that's okay, we don't need that.

00:07:21.405 --> 00:07:24.059
All right, I have some
Sanskrit words for you

00:07:24.059 --> 00:07:27.425
just to take a break and have some fun.

00:07:27.425 --> 00:07:31.175
I don't know. I have fun with Sanskrit.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:34.398
Here are some words that you could,

00:07:34.398 --> 00:07:37.837
they're going to apply very
heavily to the next section.

00:07:37.837 --> 00:07:38.992
Say: ekatva.

00:07:38.992 --> 00:07:40.217
- [Students] Ekatva.

00:07:40.217 --> 00:07:42.812
- So Sanskrit doesn't have a v,

00:07:42.812 --> 00:07:45.312
it's like a wa: ekatva.

00:07:46.909 --> 00:07:50.076
There's a @(unknown)
coming from the victory.

00:07:51.409 --> 00:07:53.777
If you know Hindi...

00:07:53.777 --> 00:07:56.151
Ekatva means one and the
same, one and together.

00:07:56.151 --> 00:07:59.149
GCIG TU 'GYUR means cause and effect

00:07:59.149 --> 00:08:01.135
have become one and the same.

00:08:01.135 --> 00:08:02.910
Cause and effect are one and the same.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:04.825
Eka means one.

00:08:04.825 --> 00:08:07.105
Ek, do, teen, chaar, panch, chhe, sat -

00:08:07.105 --> 00:08:09.114
these are Hindi.

00:08:09.114 --> 00:08:10.173
So eka means one.

00:08:10.173 --> 00:08:11.267
Ekarasa

00:08:11.267 --> 00:08:12.865
What's that?

00:08:12.865 --> 00:08:15.090
Single song. Yes.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.424
And so 'eka' came into the word ego,

00:08:17.424 --> 00:08:19.701
and from aham, you know aham?

00:08:19.701 --> 00:08:24.010
And then 'tva' is always -tion or -ness.

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:27.110
So ekatva means sameness or oneness.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:31.141
It's going to come in handy here.

00:08:31.141 --> 00:08:35.865
Are the cause and the
effect one and the same?

00:08:35.865 --> 00:08:38.831
And they're not. Right?
They're not ekatva.

00:08:38.831 --> 00:08:40.164
Okay, next word.

00:08:41.902 --> 00:08:44.902
Anyatva. And it doesn't mean onion.

00:08:46.447 --> 00:08:51.285
'Anya' means other, something
other, opposite of 'eka'.

00:08:51.285 --> 00:08:53.775
Eka means 'they're one and the same'.

00:08:53.775 --> 00:08:55.549
Anya means 'they're something else',

00:08:55.549 --> 00:08:58.799
which is an- /i - not go together.

00:09:00.257 --> 00:09:03.424
An- /i- 'don't go together'.

00:09:05.621 --> 00:09:10.016
So anyatva means 
GZHAN DU 'GYUR, something else.

00:09:10.016 --> 00:09:10.992
If they're not one,

00:09:10.992 --> 00:09:14.742
are they something
different from each other.

00:09:15.721 --> 00:09:17.048
Basically from the privative a-,

00:09:17.048 --> 00:09:19.688
privative means negative a-,

00:09:19.688 --> 00:09:21.571
it's the Greek term for it.

00:09:21.571 --> 00:09:24.571
And it's 'don't go together', anyatva,

00:09:26.207 --> 00:09:27.457
an-ya-tva.

00:09:28.769 --> 00:09:30.789
All right, next word there

00:09:30.789 --> 00:09:33.456
and there's a nice one here.

00:09:34.317 --> 00:09:35.778
Say svabhāva.

00:09:35.778 --> 00:09:36.611
- [Students] Svabhāva.

00:09:36.611 --> 00:09:39.111
- Sorry, svabhāvas.

00:09:39.993 --> 00:09:41.358
- [Students] Svabhāvas.

00:09:41.358 --> 00:09:42.388
- adbhūta.

00:09:42.388 --> 00:09:43.814
- [Students] adbhūta.

00:09:43.814 --> 00:09:44.886
- Okay, and I'm not sure

00:09:44.886 --> 00:09:46.786
that should be a long bhāva,

00:09:46.786 --> 00:09:48.255
that's what the dictionary had,

00:09:48.255 --> 00:09:51.563
but I'm suspicious a little bit.

00:09:51.563 --> 00:09:54.846
- [CK] There's two, bhāva
and bha both mean 'went'.

00:09:54.846 --> 00:09:58.250
- This one's to be, no long a.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:00.846
'Light' is long a, so I'm
suspicious of this one.

00:10:00.846 --> 00:10:02.828
But anyway that's a tradition we have.

00:10:02.828 --> 00:10:04.122
NGO BO NYID KYIS YOD PA means exist

00:10:04.122 --> 00:10:05.975
through some nature of its own.

00:10:05.975 --> 00:10:10.392
Svabhava, 'sva' means 'own',
comes from su, like suicide,

00:10:11.274 --> 00:10:15.607
to kill, 'cide' means 'kill',
like regicide or homicide.

00:10:17.661 --> 00:10:20.079
Human killing, homicide.

00:10:20.079 --> 00:10:22.496
And 'sui' means 'yourself'.

00:10:23.499 --> 00:10:26.666
So sva means self. Bhava means nature,

00:10:28.119 --> 00:10:31.126
like bhū meaning to be.

00:10:31.126 --> 00:10:33.959
So, svabhava means its own nature.

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:39.663
Adbhuta is an unusual
word that normally means

00:10:42.489 --> 00:10:46.145
'something happened,
but something amazing.'

00:10:46.145 --> 00:10:47.182
RMAD DU 'BYUNG BA

00:10:47.182 --> 00:10:50.877
in Tibetan, so adbhuta usually means,

00:10:50.877 --> 00:10:51.710
like what's the third chapter called?

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:52.543
- [Student] Practice

00:11:01.953 --> 00:11:03.053
- What's it called?

00:11:03.053 --> 00:11:04.158
- [students speaking indistinctly]

00:11:04.158 --> 00:11:05.493
- Vibhuti Padah

00:11:05.493 --> 00:11:08.355
Yes, an amazing occurrence, supposedly.

00:11:08.355 --> 00:11:09.962
We're going to talk about it.

00:11:09.962 --> 00:11:14.082
But the bhuti often means
happen, something happening,

00:11:14.082 --> 00:11:15.537
something big.

00:11:15.537 --> 00:11:18.442
Bhuti, sometimes it means something big.

00:11:18.442 --> 00:11:23.025
So here it means, svabhava
means it got its own nature,

00:11:24.488 --> 00:11:26.326
its own nature happened.

00:11:26.326 --> 00:11:27.602
NGO BO NYID KYIS YOD PA,

00:11:27.602 --> 00:11:32.519
exists through some nature of
its own, not chocolate sauce!

00:11:33.584 --> 00:11:37.065
It doesn't need chocolate
sauce for its existence.

00:11:37.065 --> 00:11:40.308
It exists as a bowl of ice cream

00:11:40.308 --> 00:11:42.271
without the chocolate sauce.

00:11:42.271 --> 00:11:44.532
So there are some words

00:11:44.532 --> 00:11:48.573
that are going to be
useful in today's class.

00:11:48.573 --> 00:11:49.406
All right.

00:11:50.362 --> 00:11:52.837
Here's the sixth option

00:11:52.837 --> 00:11:55.392
and I think we can
finish the options today,

00:11:55.392 --> 00:11:58.225
which is being refreshing somehow.

00:11:59.545 --> 00:12:00.952
Result is triggered by a cause,

00:12:00.952 --> 00:12:04.253
which is either the same
or separate from it.

00:12:04.253 --> 00:12:06.324
Is the result triggered by a cause,

00:12:06.324 --> 00:12:08.674
which is either the same as the result

00:12:08.674 --> 00:12:11.209
or separate from the result?

00:12:11.209 --> 00:12:14.559
And let's look at the possibilities.

00:12:14.559 --> 00:12:15.392
,RGYU DANG 'BRAS BU GCIG NYID DU,

00:12:15.392 --> 00:12:18.765
,NAM YANG 'THAD PAR MI 'GYUR RO,

00:12:18.765 --> 00:12:20.703
Hey, it would be ridiculous to say

00:12:20.703 --> 00:12:23.144
that the cause and the result
were exactly the same thing

00:12:23.144 --> 00:12:26.754
because why would one
start from the other.

00:12:26.754 --> 00:12:28.837
So, cancel that one.

00:12:30.562 --> 00:12:32.495
Second half of the...

00:12:32.495 --> 00:12:35.833
and by the way, he repeats
the second and fourth lines,

00:12:35.833 --> 00:12:38.025
which is Nagarjuna's style.

00:12:38.025 --> 00:12:39.346
That's ridiculous if they're one

00:12:39.346 --> 00:12:41.594
and it's ridiculous if they're separate.

00:12:41.594 --> 00:12:44.480
He's always saying that.
It's ridiculous if this,

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:47.010
and it's also ridiculous if that.

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:48.504
So NAM YANG 'THAD PA

00:12:48.504 --> 00:12:50.465
means totally big boo-boo.

00:12:50.465 --> 00:12:52.249
,RGYU DANG 'BRAS BU GZHAN NYID DU,

00:12:52.249 --> 00:12:55.481
And here's the guts.

00:12:55.481 --> 00:12:58.439
If the cause and the
effect were the same thing,

00:12:58.439 --> 00:13:00.167
then what's the point?

00:13:00.167 --> 00:13:02.755
If the cause and the effect
are totally disconnected,

00:13:02.755 --> 00:13:05.005
then what's the connection?

00:13:06.494 --> 00:13:08.819
If they are inherently different,

00:13:08.819 --> 00:13:11.086
meaning no point of contact,

00:13:11.086 --> 00:13:14.649
then why talk about cause and effect?

00:13:14.649 --> 00:13:16.950
,RGYU DANG 'BRAS BU GCIG YIN NA,

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:18.965
If the cause and the result are the same,

00:13:18.965 --> 00:13:21.311
,BSKYED BYA SKYED BYED GCIG TU 'GYUR,

00:13:21.311 --> 00:13:23.394
then what's being created

00:13:25.381 --> 00:13:28.720
and the creator are one and the same.

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:32.982
The creator and the
creation are the same thing.

00:13:32.982 --> 00:13:35.228
,RGYU DANG 'BRAS BU GZHAN NYID NA,

00:13:35.228 --> 00:13:38.516
If the cause and the effect
are essentially different,

00:13:38.516 --> 00:13:41.099
disconnectedly different,

