has to exist from its own side.

00:26:34.242 --> 00:26:37.797
We're saying, "No, let's turn it around."

00:26:37.797 --> 00:26:40.428
If the cause doesn't
exist from its own side,

00:26:40.428 --> 00:26:43.703
then the result doesn't exist
from its own side either.

00:26:43.703 --> 00:26:46.770
We kind of agree with his methodology.

00:26:46.770 --> 00:26:49.335
RGYU NYID RANG BZHIN GYIS
YOD PA 'THAD PA MA YIN NA

00:26:49.335 --> 00:26:52.615
If it's incorrect to say
that the cause itself

00:26:52.615 --> 00:26:54.890
existed through any nature of its own,

00:26:54.890 --> 00:26:55.723
'BRAS BU RANG BZHIN GYIS
YOD PA DE RGYU GANG GI

00:26:55.723 --> 00:26:56.556
YIN PAR 'GYUR

00:26:58.074 --> 00:26:58.907
then if the cause...

00:27:02.455 --> 00:27:04.142
if it's not correct to say the cause

00:27:04.142 --> 00:27:08.689
has a nature of its own,
then if a result showed up,

00:27:08.689 --> 00:27:09.772
whose is it?

00:27:12.330 --> 00:27:15.850
Sorry. If you can't say that the cause

00:27:15.850 --> 00:27:18.393
has any nature of its own,

00:27:18.393 --> 00:27:22.798
then what result that
has a nature of its own

00:27:22.798 --> 00:27:24.081
came from where, please?

00:27:24.081 --> 00:27:25.337
I'll say it again.

00:27:25.337 --> 00:27:28.524
If the cause doesn't
have a nature of its own,

00:27:28.524 --> 00:27:32.804
then where did the
self-existing result come from?

00:27:32.804 --> 00:27:33.637
Got it?

00:27:33.637 --> 00:27:36.374
If the cause doesn't
have a nature of its own

00:27:36.374 --> 00:27:39.440
and you have a result which
does have a nature of its own,

00:27:39.440 --> 00:27:43.078
then where did that result come from?

00:27:43.078 --> 00:27:46.358
Because you don't have a
cause which matches it.

00:27:46.358 --> 00:27:50.275
RGYU GANG GI YIN PAR
'GYUR BA YANG MI 'THAD

00:27:51.313 --> 00:27:53.135
What cause does the result

00:27:53.135 --> 00:27:57.552
which does have a nature
of its own belong to?

00:27:59.376 --> 00:28:02.675
If the cause can't have a
nature of its own on its own,

00:28:02.675 --> 00:28:07.094
we said in isolation,
then if you get a result

00:28:07.094 --> 00:28:08.787
that does have a nature of its own,

00:28:08.787 --> 00:28:11.177
where did it come from?

00:28:11.177 --> 00:28:13.990
Because a result that
has a nature of its own

00:28:13.990 --> 00:28:15.942
should logically come from a cause

00:28:15.942 --> 00:28:17.006
that has a nature of its own.

00:28:17.006 --> 00:28:19.544
But if you isolated the cause earlier,

00:28:19.544 --> 00:28:21.940
and said it didn't have
a nature of its own,

00:28:21.940 --> 00:28:23.445
then you got all those results

00:28:23.445 --> 00:28:25.195
that do have a nature of its own.

00:28:25.195 --> 00:28:27.212
They don't belong to anybody.

00:28:27.212 --> 00:28:30.770
They just popped out
without a cause. Got it?

00:28:30.770 --> 00:28:33.070
'BRAS BU GANG YIN PA DE 'BRAS
BU DE SKYED PA'I RGYU DE'I

00:28:33.070 --> 00:28:35.066
YIN PAR 'DOD DGOS PA'I PHYIR,

00:28:35.066 --> 00:28:37.493
Because you have to say that every result

00:28:37.493 --> 00:28:39.993
has a corresponding cause, no?

00:28:41.306 --> 00:28:44.810
So if you got a result hanging out there

00:28:44.810 --> 00:28:48.917
that did come from itself,
has its own nature,

00:28:48.917 --> 00:28:52.087
you got to find a cause that
does have its own nature

00:28:52.087 --> 00:28:54.016
to match it with.

00:28:54.016 --> 00:28:55.670
But you just said the causes

00:28:55.670 --> 00:28:57.720
don't have their own nature in isolation.

00:28:57.720 --> 00:29:01.146
Take a cause by itself, it
doesn't have its own nature.

00:29:01.146 --> 00:29:04.939
Alright, yes, we're on section three.

00:29:04.939 --> 00:29:08.856
TSOGS PA LAS SKYE BA 'GOG
PA'I RIGS PA GZHAN BSTAN PA'O,,

00:29:09.853 --> 00:29:11.616
And don't forget this outline

00:29:11.616 --> 00:29:14.592
is imposed on the book by Choney Lama.

00:29:14.592 --> 00:29:19.009
He has made up the outline
to fit the evidence.

00:29:20.002 --> 00:29:22.170
He's like a detective.

00:29:22.170 --> 00:29:26.837
He's creating a murder
scene from the blood spots.

00:29:28.440 --> 00:29:31.171
So he's imposing a structure on the text,

00:29:31.171 --> 00:29:33.955
which is extremely helpful.

00:29:33.955 --> 00:29:37.622
And so far, I'd say I vote for it 100%.

00:29:38.729 --> 00:29:42.738
I've seen books where the
author pushed it too far

00:29:42.738 --> 00:29:47.738
to get their outline in, but
this one seems to work to me.

00:29:47.882 --> 00:29:49.894
So the third part here is:

00:29:49.894 --> 00:29:51.993
TSOGS PA LAS SKYE BA 'GOG
PA'I RIGS PA GZHAN BSTAN PA'O,,

00:29:51.993 --> 00:29:53.845
I'll give you more reasons

00:29:53.845 --> 00:29:56.154
why a result doesn't come about

00:29:56.154 --> 00:30:00.103
through the coming together
of causes and conditions.

00:30:00.103 --> 00:30:01.401
I'll give you another reason

00:30:01.401 --> 00:30:04.877
why results don't pop out of circumstances

00:30:04.877 --> 00:30:07.076
where you have causes and
conditions coming together,

00:30:07.076 --> 00:30:10.993
because that's the one
that we most want to be.

00:30:12.233 --> 00:30:14.748
That's the one that feels
most comfortable to us.

00:30:14.748 --> 00:30:16.595
Look, Geshe-la,

00:30:16.595 --> 00:30:18.405
the seed is there, the water is there,

00:30:18.405 --> 00:30:21.747
and the sunlight is there,
and the gardener is there,

00:30:21.747 --> 00:30:24.997
fertilize it, then it's going to come out.

00:30:26.340 --> 00:30:28.243
The tree is going to come out.

00:30:28.243 --> 00:30:30.366
In fact, we had huge
debates in the monastery

00:30:30.366 --> 00:30:34.645
of whether it was even possible
to reverse it at that point.

00:30:34.645 --> 00:30:38.195
In the millisecond before
the result comes out,

00:30:38.195 --> 00:30:42.020
is it possible to cancel
a result coming out

00:30:42.020 --> 00:30:44.792
if all the conditions are present?

00:30:44.792 --> 00:30:48.751
And the famous answer is,
"Yes." And we're like, "Why?"

00:30:48.751 --> 00:30:53.751
And he says, "If a crow flies
down and picks up the seed?"

00:30:53.971 --> 00:30:56.403
[laughing]

00:30:56.403 --> 00:30:58.125
And you're all like...

00:30:58.125 --> 00:31:00.709
[students laughing]

00:31:00.709 --> 00:31:02.737
You, guys, can think about that one.

00:31:02.737 --> 00:31:06.237
It's supposedly an ancient valid argument.

00:31:08.055 --> 00:31:09.339
I think then you'd say the causes

00:31:09.339 --> 00:31:11.471
and the conditions weren't there.

00:31:11.471 --> 00:31:13.018
Because the condition of the seed

00:31:13.018 --> 00:31:16.588
sitting in the dirt wasn't there anymore.

00:31:16.588 --> 00:31:19.733
I would say, but it's a famous,

00:31:19.733 --> 00:31:23.159
I don't know, the abbot was
just like...[scratches head]

00:31:23.159 --> 00:31:24.978
I remember the debate.

00:31:24.978 --> 00:31:26.930
TSOGS PA LAS SKYE BA 'GOG
PA'I RIGS PA GZHAN BSTAN PA'O,,

00:31:26.930 --> 00:31:29.430
Let's talk about other reasons

00:31:30.330 --> 00:31:34.497
why results don't pop out
of, what did we call it?

00:31:35.482 --> 00:31:37.103
I'll give you five dollars.

00:31:37.103 --> 00:31:38.270
The consummate

00:31:40.204 --> 00:31:41.037
convening.

00:31:42.580 --> 00:31:44.295
That's my word.

00:31:44.295 --> 00:31:48.034
I'm going to use it as
the name of my next band.

00:31:48.034 --> 00:31:50.382
The Consummate Convening.

00:31:50.382 --> 00:31:53.382
Anyway, try to struggle to imagine

00:31:55.112 --> 00:31:58.033
all the necessary causes and conditions

00:31:58.033 --> 00:32:00.177
have already come together.

00:32:00.177 --> 00:32:02.081
The sugar's there. The flour's
there. The milk's there.

00:32:02.081 --> 00:32:06.748
The oven's on. The time
passed. the cake is made.

00:32:08.523 --> 00:32:11.361
So we're going to have
a few final arguments

00:32:11.361 --> 00:32:14.024
about why we don't like that.

00:32:14.024 --> 00:32:16.165
,RGYU RNAMS DANG NI RKYEN DAG GI,

00:32:16.165 --> 00:32:18.073
,TSOGS PA GANG YIN DE YIS NI,

00:32:18.073 --> 00:32:19.331
,BDAG GIS BDAG NYID MI SKYED NA,

00:32:19.331 --> 00:32:22.014
,'BRAS BU JI LTAR SKYED PAR BYED,

00:32:22.014 --> 00:32:24.680
If you assembled all the necessary causes

00:32:24.680 --> 00:32:29.097
and conditions, and it
couldn't produce itself,

00:32:33.233 --> 00:32:37.900
if the causes and the conditions, if the
water, the sunlight, the seed,

00:32:39.561 --> 00:32:43.383
the gardener, and the fertilizer
couldn't create the water,

00:32:43.383 --> 00:32:46.159
the sunlight, the gardener.

00:32:46.159 --> 00:32:49.367
If all the causes couldn't
create themselves,

00:32:49.367 --> 00:32:50.200
'BRAS BU JI LTAR

00:32:50.200 --> 00:32:53.617
then how could they cause something else?

00:32:58.181 --> 00:33:01.661
We need a commentary,
right? I'll say it again.

00:33:01.661 --> 00:33:05.712
If the seed, water,
fertilizer, gardener, sunlight

00:33:05.712 --> 00:33:10.594
didn't create the seed,
water, gardener, sunlight,

00:33:10.594 --> 00:33:14.511
then how could they all
together create a tree?

00:33:15.536 --> 00:33:18.210
We need a commentary. Here we go.

00:33:18.210 --> 00:33:19.348
,DE PHYIR TSOGS LAS BYAS BA MIN,

00:33:19.348 --> 00:33:22.103
Therefore, the result is not created

00:33:22.103 --> 00:33:24.812
by the convening of the
causes and conditions.

00:33:24.812 --> 00:33:27.084
,TSOGS MIN BYAS PA'I 'BRAS BU'ANG MED,

00:33:27.084 --> 00:33:29.294
And if you never had the causes
and the conditions together,

00:33:29.294 --> 00:33:32.626
that wouldn't create the result either.

00:33:32.626 --> 00:33:35.125
,'BRAS BU YOD PA MA YIN NA,

00:33:35.125 --> 00:33:35.988
If there's no result,

00:33:35.988 --> 00:33:38.259
,RKYEN GYI TSOGS PA GA LA YOD,

00:33:38.259 --> 00:33:42.259
then how can you say all
the conditions collected?

00:33:44.008 --> 00:33:46.761
That's that retroactive,
you get to be a cause

00:33:46.761 --> 00:33:49.971
because now you produced a result. Got it?

00:33:49.971 --> 00:33:51.940
All right, here we go.

00:33:51.940 --> 00:33:52.773
[clapping]

00:33:52.773 --> 00:33:55.516
RGYUS RKYEN TSOGS NAS
'BRAS BU SKYED DO ZHE NA,

00:33:55.516 --> 00:33:57.825
And this is very
reasonable, somebody says,

00:33:57.825 --> 00:33:59.972
"Look, you want a result,

00:33:59.972 --> 00:34:02.235
just put together all the
causes and conditions,

00:34:02.235 --> 00:34:05.463
and the result will pop out.
That's the way it works."

00:34:05.463 --> 00:34:06.463
Then we say,

00:34:07.486 --> 00:34:11.652
RGYU RKYEN GYI TSOGS PA BDAG
GIS BDAG NYID NI MI SKYED DE,

00:34:11.652 --> 00:34:14.346
But don't you agree
that the coming together

00:34:14.346 --> 00:34:16.047
of the conditions and causes

00:34:16.047 --> 00:34:19.319
have not created the
conditions and causes?

00:34:19.319 --> 00:34:21.867
Yes, that's okay. We can agree.

00:34:21.867 --> 00:34:25.361
Fertilizer didn't give
birth to the fertilizer.

00:34:25.361 --> 00:34:28.477
'BRAS BU SKYE BA DON MED
PA DANG RANG LA BYED PA

00:34:28.477 --> 00:34:30.135
'GAL BA DANG TSOGS PA RDZAS
SU MED PA'I PHYIR RO,,

00:34:30.135 --> 00:34:35.135
Three reasons here, and
one of them is interesting.

00:34:35.200 --> 00:34:37.127
Personally.

00:34:37.127 --> 00:34:37.960
Here we go.

00:34:37.960 --> 00:34:40.774
RGYU RKYEN GYI TSOGS PA

00:34:40.774 --> 00:34:43.321
When the causes and
conditions come together,

00:34:43.321 --> 00:34:45.533
BDAG GIS BDAG NYID NI MI SKYED DE,

00:34:45.533 --> 00:34:49.437
they don't themselves create themselves.

00:34:49.437 --> 00:34:50.270
Why?

00:34:50.270 --> 00:34:52.989
'BRAS BU SKYE BA DON MED PA

00:34:52.989 --> 00:34:55.468
If the causes and conditions
could come together

00:34:55.468 --> 00:34:57.452
and create the causes and conditions,

00:34:57.452 --> 00:35:00.187
then there would be no need for them

00:35:00.187 --> 00:35:03.759
to create something else, like a result.

00:35:03.759 --> 00:35:04.592
MED PA DANG

00:35:04.592 --> 00:35:07.178
That's kind of weird.

00:35:07.178 --> 00:35:08.011
Second reason.

00:35:08.011 --> 00:35:11.928
RANG LA BYED PA 'GAL BA

00:35:15.848 --> 00:35:19.490
It's a contradiction to say
that something created itself.

00:35:19.490 --> 00:35:20.490
That's okay.

00:35:21.569 --> 00:35:23.077
We can't say the seed created the seed

00:35:23.077 --> 00:35:24.385
or something like that,
unless you're talking

00:35:24.385 --> 00:35:28.386
about the continuing of the seed itself.

00:35:28.386 --> 00:35:32.951
But I like the last one, and
I want to talk about that.

00:35:32.951 --> 00:35:35.690
TSOGS PA RDZAS SU MED PA'I PHYIR

00:35:35.690 --> 00:35:37.000
And this word RDZAS in Tibetan,

00:35:37.000 --> 00:35:40.603
'dravya' in Sanskrit.

00:35:40.603 --> 00:35:42.353
Substance, substance.

00:35:43.288 --> 00:35:47.121
It's a highly debated
word in all the schools.

00:35:49.413 --> 00:35:54.413
So RDZAS means stuff.

00:35:54.714 --> 00:35:55.547
He says,

00:35:58.801 --> 00:36:02.016
"Conventions of causes and conditions

00:36:02.016 --> 00:36:04.782
are not RDZAS."

00:36:04.782 --> 00:36:07.282
So they can't create other thing.

00:36:10.329 --> 00:36:14.543
They're not substantial
enough to create something.

00:36:14.543 --> 00:36:17.827
Not the causes and conditions separately,

00:36:17.827 --> 00:36:21.027
and not the causes and
conditions together,

00:36:21.027 --> 00:36:25.041
but the convening doesn't make the result.

00:36:25.041 --> 00:36:27.929
The convening is just the situation,

00:36:27.929 --> 00:36:29.846
it's not a stuff.

00:36:31.329 --> 00:36:33.788
The coming together, the
act of coming together

00:36:33.788 --> 00:36:37.155
is not stuff, and since it's not stuff,

00:36:37.155 --> 00:36:39.350
it doesn't produce anything.

00:36:39.350 --> 00:36:42.534
So I don't want to say the coming together

00:36:42.534 --> 00:36:45.521
of the causes and
conditions created the tree.

00:36:45.521 --> 00:36:47.235
I don't want to say that. Why?

00:36:47.235 --> 00:36:49.859
Coming together is just
kind of like an idea.

00:36:49.859 --> 00:36:52.495
It's not the actual things.

00:36:52.495 --> 00:36:57.121
It's their being in the
same area at the same time.

00:36:57.121 --> 00:37:00.200
That's not big enough to make a tree.

00:37:00.200 --> 00:37:02.595
Causes and conditions
being in the same area

00:37:02.595 --> 00:37:05.707
at the same time is not solid enough

00:37:05.707 --> 00:37:09.707
to create a two ton tree.
It's just a condition.

00:37:10.936 --> 00:37:13.875
I like that one. It's kind of interesting.

00:37:13.875 --> 00:37:17.792
TSOGS PA RDZAS SU MED PAS
RANG GIS BDAG NYID MI SKYED NA

00:37:19.290 --> 00:37:22.830
Since the coming together
of causes and conditions

00:37:22.830 --> 00:37:26.591
is not like a solid thing of its own,

00:37:26.591 --> 00:37:29.841
not like chemicals and nutrients,

00:37:31.493 --> 00:37:34.951
MED PAS BDAG NYID MI SKYED NA

00:37:34.951 --> 00:37:38.297
if that means it can't produce something,

00:37:38.297 --> 00:37:42.227
DES JI LTAR NA 'BRAS BU RANG
BZHIN GYIS SKYED PAR BYED DE,

00:37:42.227 --> 00:37:46.394
If the coming together is
not a solid enough thing

00:37:48.117 --> 00:37:51.069
to create the result,

00:37:51.069 --> 00:37:53.486
then how could it ever create

00:37:55.716 --> 00:37:57.299
a result by itself?

00:37:58.559 --> 00:38:00.990
It would be like 
MO GSHAM GYI BU

00:38:00.990 --> 00:38:04.129
300 dollars 
MO GSHAM GYI BU.

00:38:04.129 --> 00:38:05.379
MO GSHAM GYI BU

00:38:07.285 --> 00:38:08.535
It's an idiom.

00:38:09.463 --> 00:38:12.546
It means the child of a barren woman.

00:38:13.667 --> 00:38:16.531
Famous expression. I don't know.

00:38:16.531 --> 00:38:20.049
A child of a woman who lost
her ovaries or something.

00:38:20.049 --> 00:38:23.363
That's just not possible,
not a possibility.

00:38:23.363 --> 00:38:25.584
What's not possible?

00:38:25.584 --> 00:38:29.142
If the coming together
itself is not concrete enough

00:38:29.142 --> 00:38:31.392
to produce a result,

00:38:32.416 --> 00:38:35.808
then how can you guys be saying

00:38:35.808 --> 00:38:40.141
that the convening
self-existently creates a result?

00:38:41.766 --> 00:38:43.960
If the coming together,

00:38:43.960 --> 00:38:46.255
not the chemicals, not the
seeds, not the fertilizer,

00:38:46.255 --> 00:38:47.735
not the warmth of the sun,

00:38:47.735 --> 00:38:49.958
but the action of coming together,

00:38:49.958 --> 00:38:52.643
If that's not enough of stuff or of things

00:38:52.643 --> 00:38:54.902
to create a result,
then why are you talking

00:38:54.902 --> 00:38:58.139
about some kind of
self-existent creating a result,

00:38:58.139 --> 00:39:01.339
if it's not even a normal
creating of result.

00:39:01.339 --> 00:39:02.321
Got it?

00:39:02.321 --> 00:39:05.055
Because their original
argument in this section

00:39:05.055 --> 00:39:07.683
was the coming together
of causes and conditions

00:39:07.683 --> 00:39:09.059
creates the result.

00:39:09.059 --> 00:39:09.976
We say, "No."

00:39:10.869 --> 00:39:13.735
Would we say the causes and
conditions create the result?

00:39:13.735 --> 00:39:14.856
Yes.

00:39:14.856 --> 00:39:16.980
[coughing]

00:39:16.980 --> 00:39:18.487
Would we say the coming together

00:39:18.487 --> 00:39:20.565
of the causes and conditions
creates the result?

00:39:20.565 --> 00:39:22.815
No, that's too theoretical.

00:39:23.775 --> 00:39:25.308
Would we say the coming together

00:39:25.308 --> 00:39:27.493
of the causes and conditions
creates the result

00:39:27.493 --> 00:39:29.096
if the coming together itself

00:39:29.096 --> 00:39:31.355
exists through some nature of its own?

00:39:31.355 --> 00:39:33.987
We say, "That's something
you made up anyway."

00:39:33.987 --> 00:39:36.705
[laughing]

00:39:36.705 --> 00:39:37.622
All right.

00:39:40.075 --> 00:39:41.875
I took a picture. I was trying to...

00:39:41.875 --> 00:39:46.286
Now look, you got to realize
what I was trying to do.

00:39:46.286 --> 00:39:49.281
I was trying to create a
picture of multiple elements

00:39:49.281 --> 00:39:52.941
that didn't have a common purpose.

00:39:52.941 --> 00:39:56.435
And it was just a crowd
walking down the street.

00:39:56.435 --> 00:40:00.062
They're not walking to build
a snowman or something.

00:40:00.062 --> 00:40:03.127
They're just walking down
the street in New York.

00:40:03.127 --> 00:40:05.873
They don't have a goal in mind.

00:40:05.873 --> 00:40:08.021
The walking of people down the street

00:40:08.021 --> 00:40:09.809
doesn't create a snowman.

00:40:09.809 --> 00:40:13.314
The people do, if they choose
to go to Lincoln Center,

00:40:13.314 --> 00:40:16.857
I think, Lincoln Center Ice Rink.

00:40:16.857 --> 00:40:19.777
But if they don't, then
they're just a bunch of people

00:40:19.777 --> 00:40:24.110
walking by 5th Avenue up
near John's favorite place.

00:40:25.113 --> 00:40:27.363
What was that place called?

00:40:31.404 --> 00:40:35.403
No, on the park, the department store?

00:40:35.403 --> 00:40:38.305
[students speaking indistinctly]

00:40:38.305 --> 00:40:39.323
- [Students] Bergdorf's?

00:40:39.323 --> 00:40:41.558
- Bergdorf, yes, yes, yes.

00:40:41.558 --> 00:40:43.705
Okay, we're not going to talk about it.

00:40:43.705 --> 00:40:45.765
I'm being discreet.

00:40:45.765 --> 00:40:48.264
DE'I PHYIR RGYU RKYEN GYI
TSOGS PA LAS BYAS PA'I 'BRAS BU

00:40:48.264 --> 00:40:49.847
NGO BO NYID KYIS YOD PA MA YIN NO,,

00:40:51.785 --> 00:40:53.391
We have some time, right?

00:40:53.391 --> 00:40:54.658
What time we got to stop?

00:40:54.658 --> 00:40:56.058
- [Tim] In five minutes.

00:40:56.058 --> 00:40:58.073
- Okay, five minutes, we've got just time.

00:40:58.073 --> 00:40:59.185
What've we got here?

00:40:59.185 --> 00:41:02.021
RANG LUGS

00:41:02.021 --> 00:41:04.354
He's finally, not Nagarjuna,

00:41:05.228 --> 00:41:06.061
but Choney Lama's going to
say, "Well, what do we think?

00:41:06.061 --> 00:41:06.894
I'll tell you what we think."

00:41:11.250 --> 00:41:13.468
Yay! You should stand up more often

00:41:13.468 --> 00:41:15.184
and tell us about what you think.

00:41:15.184 --> 00:41:16.605
[laughing]

00:41:16.605 --> 00:41:17.438
Oh, here's.

00:41:17.438 --> 00:41:19.923
RGYU RKYEN TSOGS PA LAS 'BRAS BU SKYE YANG

00:41:19.923 --> 00:41:23.081
We, in our system, we do agree

00:41:23.081 --> 00:41:25.865
that when the causes and
conditions come together,

00:41:25.865 --> 00:41:27.039
they do produce a result.

00:41:27.039 --> 00:41:29.318
We can say that in Madhyamika,

00:41:29.318 --> 00:41:31.639
we can say that. That's okay.

00:41:31.639 --> 00:41:32.472
KYANG, 
but

00:41:36.339 --> 00:41:37.560
TSOGS PA BRDZUN PAS

00:41:37.560 --> 00:41:41.477
But the idea, but the
concept of the collection

00:41:42.935 --> 00:41:45.518
or the convening is artificial.

00:41:48.770 --> 00:41:52.096
Because it's BRDZUN
BRDZUN means a lie.

00:41:52.096 --> 00:41:54.763
But what he means is 'artificial'.

00:41:56.930 --> 00:42:01.266
The coming together of causes
and conditions is artificial.

00:42:01.266 --> 00:42:03.518
It's an artificial concept.

00:42:03.518 --> 00:42:06.531
The causes may be solid.
The conditions may be solid.

00:42:06.531 --> 00:42:09.510
But the coming together
is sort of like an opinion

00:42:09.510 --> 00:42:10.343
or something.

00:42:10.343 --> 00:42:13.501
BRDZUN PAS 'BRAS BU YANG
BRDZUN PA SKYED PAR BYED PA

00:42:13.501 --> 00:42:16.881
Now, if you want to say
it this way, I'll buy it.

00:42:16.881 --> 00:42:18.548
Who's that? Who's I?

00:42:19.820 --> 00:42:20.653
Choney Lama.

00:42:20.653 --> 00:42:24.153
If you want to say it
this way, I'll buy it.

00:42:28.361 --> 00:42:31.358
An artificial convention of people

00:42:31.358 --> 00:42:34.500
could create an artificial
result. That's okay.

00:42:34.500 --> 00:42:36.687
I'll buy that.

00:42:36.687 --> 00:42:38.697
An artificial coming together,

00:42:38.697 --> 00:42:41.629
chocolate coated coming together,

00:42:41.629 --> 00:42:45.379
if it created an artificial
result of a tree,

00:42:46.801 --> 00:42:48.190
that's chocolate coated,

00:42:48.190 --> 00:42:52.300
and the whole thing was
chocolate coated, I'll buy it.

00:42:52.300 --> 00:42:53.351
Got it?

00:42:53.351 --> 00:42:54.769
Then I'm okay with it.

00:42:54.769 --> 00:42:57.157
If you mean artificial
trees, artificial causes,

00:42:57.157 --> 00:43:00.717
artificial coming together
creates an artificial tree,

00:43:00.717 --> 00:43:01.838
I'm okay with it.

00:43:01.838 --> 00:43:03.601
Hey, what do you mean by artificial?

00:43:03.601 --> 00:43:08.601
I mean it's coming from
me. It's not real out there.

00:43:08.631 --> 00:43:12.461
It didn't exist before I
was there. I created it.

00:43:12.461 --> 00:43:13.378
Cool.

00:43:15.018 --> 00:43:19.999
He's got one more sentence,
It's okay? We got time.

00:43:19.999 --> 00:43:22.082
RGYU RKYEN GYI TSOGS PA
MIN PAS BYAS PA'I 'BRAS

00:43:22.082 --> 00:43:23.779
BU'ANG MED DE,

00:43:23.779 --> 00:43:27.316
By the way, I'm not saying
you could ever have a result

00:43:27.316 --> 00:43:29.974
if the causes and the
conditions didn't get together.

00:43:29.974 --> 00:43:32.711
I didn't say that. That's
not what I'm saying.

00:43:32.711 --> 00:43:35.224
DE NI SHIN TU YANG 'GAL BA'I PHYIR,

00:43:35.224 --> 00:43:37.516
You guys know 
SHIN TU.

00:43:37.516 --> 00:43:39.844
That's total crap.

00:43:39.844 --> 00:43:43.189
It's like, your stuff is regular crap,

00:43:43.189 --> 00:43:44.829
but to say they don't create anything,

00:43:44.829 --> 00:43:48.361
now that's total crap.
He's like really funny.

00:43:48.361 --> 00:43:50.444
SHIN TU is completely BS.

00:43:52.923 --> 00:43:57.256
Your usual stuff about
self-existence is pretty lame.

00:43:58.470 --> 00:44:01.966
But if you want me to say that I'm saying

00:44:01.966 --> 00:44:04.788
that they don't produce a
result when they come together,

00:44:04.788 --> 00:44:08.371
that's ridiculous. I never said that.

00:44:09.506 --> 00:44:10.637
One more line.

00:44:10.637 --> 00:44:14.295
Oh, by the way, and then
we finish the chapter. Yay!

00:44:14.295 --> 00:44:16.662
And then we've got one more
chapter to go for this course,

00:44:16.662 --> 00:44:20.171
which is going to be 22
if I'm not mistaken, 21.

00:44:20.171 --> 00:44:21.806
Okay, here we go.

00:44:21.806 --> 00:44:24.781
JI SKAD BSHAD PA'I RIGS PAS
RNAM PAR DPYAD PA NA 'BRAS BU

00:44:24.781 --> 00:44:27.481
RANG BZHIN GYIS YOD PA MA YIN
NA RGYU RKYEN GYI TSOGS PA

00:44:27.481 --> 00:44:29.606
RANG BZHIN GYIS GA LA YOD,

00:44:29.606 --> 00:44:34.606
If you follow the arguments
I've been making in this chapter

00:44:34.730 --> 00:44:38.730
and if we can say that
the result that comes out

00:44:40.693 --> 00:44:44.310
is not something that could
exist in and of itself,

00:44:44.310 --> 00:44:47.310
then you'd have to logically believe

00:44:48.559 --> 00:44:51.878
that the coming together of
the causes and conditions

00:44:51.878 --> 00:44:54.415
was also not something
that existed by itself.

00:44:54.415 --> 00:44:56.122
That's all I'm trying to say.

00:44:56.122 --> 00:44:58.230
I'm trying to point out to you guys

00:44:58.230 --> 00:44:59.923
that if the result is not something

00:44:59.923 --> 00:45:01.779
that could exist by itself,

00:45:01.779 --> 00:45:04.192
then the coming together
of causes and conditions

00:45:04.192 --> 00:45:06.734
that created that result, logically,

00:45:06.734 --> 00:45:07.948
would have to be the same.

00:45:07.948 --> 00:45:09.834
They could not be coming
from their own side.

00:45:09.834 --> 00:45:12.251
They must be coming from you.

00:45:13.840 --> 00:45:16.384
The fertilizer is coming from you.

00:45:16.384 --> 00:45:19.001
The water is coming from you.

00:45:19.001 --> 00:45:21.194
The fact that the gardener showed up

00:45:21.194 --> 00:45:23.306
is coming from you.

00:45:23.306 --> 00:45:27.546
The fact that the sun shone
today is coming from you,

00:45:27.546 --> 00:45:29.918
if the tree is coming from you.

00:45:29.918 --> 00:45:30.751
Got it?

00:45:30.751 --> 00:45:33.076
It's kind of cute.

00:45:33.076 --> 00:45:34.817
GA LA YOD, RGYU 'BRAS GNYIS RANG 
BZHIN GYIS YOD MED MTSUNGS PA'I

00:45:35.675 --> 00:45:38.508
Because it should all be the same.

00:45:40.123 --> 00:45:41.621
Whatever's true of the collection

00:45:41.621 --> 00:45:42.963
should be true of the tree.

00:45:42.963 --> 00:45:43.929
Whatever's true of the tree

00:45:43.929 --> 00:45:47.096
should be true of the coming together.

00:45:47.096 --> 00:45:48.846
Yay! Onto chapter 21,

00:45:49.876 --> 00:45:51.486
which is called

00:45:51.486 --> 00:45:55.918
'An Investigation of How Things
Occur and Then Pass Away.'

00:45:55.918 --> 00:46:00.917
An Investigation of How Things
Occur and Then Pass Away.

00:46:00.917 --> 00:46:03.137
So that's a new topic.

00:46:03.137 --> 00:46:07.111
Yay! See you tomorrow.
Hold onto your hats.

